From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:05:30 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] qwen3_5: an MTP hold prices as a fixed cost of a
 drafted shared round (TF_MTP_FIXED_HOLD)

Shared prices fit a drafted round's excess over the plain point as a per-row slope. An MTP hold costs
about the same however few drafts it holds, so few rows made the slope steep, the allocator cut drafts,
and the next fit was steeper: 8 short chats settled 11-17% below plain decode after the first wave.
With hold_fixed, every drafting round's extra rows and residual feed a decayed least-squares fit: its
intercept is a fixed cost of any drafting round (the hold), its slope what a row costs past the forward
table at this context. Off by default (Model.hold_fixed).
